Imports:
  - Types:
      - AbstractHttpAdapter
    From: packages/core/adapters
  - Types:
      - BadRequestException
      - InternalServerErrorException
    From: packages/common/exceptions

Annotations: |
  Concrete `AbstractHttpAdapter` implementation over the Express HTTP library: the
  default HTTP platform used by the Express platform package.

---

"AbstractHttpAdapter::ExpressAdapter(instance: any)":
  location: express-adapter.ts
  annotations: |
    Wraps an Express application (or an externally supplied one) behind the
    `AbstractHttpAdapter` contract from Imports.

    `instance`: an existing Express app, or undefined to create a new one

    Algorithm:
    1. Register a root-level middleware that runs the configured request/response
       hooks around every request, ahead of any route-specific middleware
  methods:
    "reply(response: any, body: any, statusCode: number)": |
      Send `body` as the Express response. A streamable-file body is piped as a
      stream with its headers applied; otherwise an object body is sent as JSON,
      anything else as a plain string.
    "setErrorHandler(handler: Object<string, any>, prefix: string)": |
      Mount `handler` as Express error-handling middleware, both under `prefix` (if
      given) and at the application root, so routes outside the prefix still reach
      it.
    "setNotFoundHandler(handler: Object<string, any>, prefix: string)": |
      Mount `handler` as a catch-all Express route. When `prefix` is given, requests
      outside that prefix are passed through instead of being treated as not found,
      so multiple prefixed Nest apps can share one Express instance.
    "normalizePath(path: string) -> path: string": |
      Convert legacy Express route syntax to a form the underlying path-matching
      library accepts, raising a descriptive error for patterns Express's stricter
      router rejects.
    "applyVersionFilter(handler: Object<string, any>, version: string | Array<string>, versioningOptions: Object<string, any>) -> filtered: Object<string, any>": |
      Build a request handler that only forwards to `handler` when the request's
      version (from the URI, a header, the Accept media type, or a custom extractor)
      matches `version`; otherwise calls through to the next handler. Throws
      `InternalServerErrorException` from Imports if invoked with no further handler
      to fall back to.
    "mapException(error: any) -> mapped: any": |
      Convert an Express body-parser syntax or URI error into a `BadRequestException`
      from Imports; every other error passes through unchanged.
    "initHttpServer(options: Object<string, any>)": |
      Create a Node HTTP or HTTPS server (based on `options`) wrapping the Express
      instance, optionally rejecting new requests while shutting down.

